25,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"It seems our past successes are tied to accessibility, though some older blocks hide nasty surprises that delay progress.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The demand for general space is overwhelming, while specialist rooms sit empty. Also, off-site hiring costs for displaced rooms are significant.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,George,,"Our grounds staff is depleted, yet technicians are underutilized. More concerningly, the bench staff are wasting hours on manual ventilation checks.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Comfort-based projects are notorious for slipping by a year, and outdoor work is frequently crippled by weather delays.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Mechanical costs are climbing sharply, and we have a glaring lack of reserves for replacing aging audiovisual equipment.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"These findings suggest we should avoid projects that are purely for ""comfort"" or located in problematic old blocks.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Victoria,,Exactly. We need something that addresses the general room shortage without causing a timetable crisis.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,George,,The manual burden on technicians is a point of failure. We need a solution that reduces that daily grind.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"If we choose an outdoor project, we risk a massive schedule slip due to the weather and historical trends.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,And we must consider that mechanical upgrades will be more expensive than the initial estimates suggest.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
